WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.790
Where does a great idea come from?

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:13.150
In my experience, it all starts with a single spark.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:21.910
That's how we became the creatures of the night.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.110
Something small, but bright.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.110
Maybe something only visible to one person.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.490
Hush, little one.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.030
Let me sing you to sleep.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.750
Moonlight has come,

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.780
Now, drift off to a dream.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.180
That might be something. Did you get that
one?

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.820
Guys! Wake up! Don and Clifford going to

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.670
be here in an hour. Jesus.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.130
Howard, what do we have for our producers?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.230
We have one complete song, 11 fragments, and
25 rough notions screamed over piano chords.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.470
Maybe one night wasn't enough time to
write a whole show.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.460
Are you kidding?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.960
One night in 1978, I wrote two
musicals in George Plimpton's bathroom.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.920
Or was it one musical in two nights? It's all
pretty hazy. The point is, Norman Mailer

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.760
punched me in the mouth, and when I woke up,
I was in Betty Friedan's waterbed.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:30.810
I love that story. Hey, Oliver. Quick crazy thought. My cousin, Moses Morris, he's very big at State Farm insurance.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.870
Howard, did you notice how when I told a
story, it had recognizable names and a point?

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:37.110
No.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.360
Moses Morris runs sponsorships for State
Farm. So let's say I gave him a ring. Maybe

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.230
they sponsor the musical, and then we don't
even need Donna and Cliff. Bam!

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.450
We don't need your- Moses Morris?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.830
Yeah.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.010
Everything we need is right here.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.560
Look at this cast.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.510
They're all killers.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.290
As we look at the cast, we are faced with an
unsettling truth. Any one of them could be

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.020
the killer.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:07.740
Any notes?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.670
Oliver always gives me notes on my reads.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.640
I thought it was fine.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.300
Oh, Oliver would be a little more snarky.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.460
Do you want me to- Okay.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.700
Excellent. Charles. This time, try it with a
dash of none of what you just did.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.630
Oh, yeah.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.100
Oh, God, I miss him.

